  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and eccentricity of ellipse is <math><mi>e</mi></math><br />then <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math><br />(where <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> is&nbsp;length of major axis)<br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo>